# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: On the final night, with the swollen crone of the moon filling the whole sky above the rooftops, the Ghostlight Express pulls in one last time.
Narrator: The Vagrant holds the carriage door open against the trembling wind, and you step aboard as the lanterns of Wickermoor flicker below.
Narrator: Iron wheels scream against the track as the engine gathers speed, racing out across the shaking trestle at the edge of the moor.
Narrator: Behind the last car, the sky splits open in blinding white silence as the moon finally comes down upon the valley of Druskenvald.
Narrator: A shock of cold wind rattles the windowpanes, carrying a last scatter of oak leaves and ash past the glass.
the_vagrant [sad]: Keep your eyes toward the engine, friends, for there is nothing left behind us that bears looking at twice.
Narrator: He keeps his hand tight on the throttle and never turns his head as the train crosses into the pale grey safety of the Shroud.
-> END
